{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSumElasticity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSumElasticity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.StaircaseHookMultiset"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.staircase_hookSum_eq_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.staircase_hookSum_eq_iff","kind":"theorem","line":256,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HookSumElasticity.lean#L256-L304","doc":"**And uniquely.**  Equality forces every displacement to vanish, so `ν` has the staircase's\nrow lengths throughout the frame — the hook sum's minimiser at triangular size is the staircase\nand nothing else. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.staircase_hookSum_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.staircase_hookSum_le","kind":"theorem","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HookSumElasticity.lean#L238-L254","doc":"**The staircase minimises the hook sum** at its own size.  Both terms of the deficiency are\nnon-negative — the first by `staircase_bracket_term_nonneg`, the second because it is a sum of\nsquares — and no frame restriction is needed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.staircase_two_mul_hookSum_sub_of_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.staircase_two_mul_hookSum_sub_of_le","kind":"theorem","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HookSumElasticity.lean#L206-L234","doc":"**In a frame of `k + 1` rows the linear term is absent outright**, and the deficiency is a\nbare sum of squares:\n\n    2 ( H(ν) − H_min )  =  Σ_{i<k+1} u_i² .\n\nThis is the sharp form the `REV_n` arc uses, and it is what makes the cost *quantised*: with\n`Σ u_i = 0` the right-hand side is an even integer, so `H − H_min ∈ ℤ_{≥0}`.  It needs\n`ν.colLen 0 ≤ k + 1`; a taller shape has the same hook multiset as its transpose, so the\ngeneral form above covers it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.staircase_two_mul_hookSum_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.staircase_two_mul_hookSum_sub","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HookSumElasticity.lean#L164-L204","doc":"**The hook sum's deficiency above the staircase, exactly.**  For every `ν` of the staircase's\nsize, in any frame containing both,\n\n    2 ( H(ν) − H(δ_k) )  =  Σ_{i<L} 2(i − k)·u_i  +  Σ_{i<L} u_i² ,\n\nwith `u_i = β_i(ν) − β_i(δ_k) = λ_i(ν) − λ_i(δ_k)` and truncated subtraction in `(i − k)`.  An\nidentity, not a bound: no term of the expansion is discarded and `ν` may be arbitrarily far from\nthe staircase. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.staircase_bracket_term_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.staircase_bracket_term_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HookSumElasticity.lean#L143-L160","doc":"Where the staircase's bracket is not constant — the rows `i > k`, which `δ_k` does not\nreach — the displacement is `ν`'s own row length, hence non-negative.  Elsewhere the factor is\nzero.  Either way the product is `≥ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.staircase_colLen_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.staircase_colLen_zero","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HookSumElasticity.lean#L138-L141","doc":"The staircase reaches exactly `k` rows, so every frame with `k ≤ L` contains it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.staircase_bracket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.staircase_bracket","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HookSumElasticity.lean#L128-L136","doc":"**The staircase's bracket, in any frame:** `r_i = (2k + 1) + 2·(i − k)`, with truncated\nsubtraction, so the second term vanishes for `i ≤ k`.  The `L` cancels — which is the reason the\nminimality below needs no restriction on the padding. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.betaR_sub_eq_rowLen_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.betaR_sub_eq_rowLen_sub","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HookSumElasticity.lean#L118-L124","doc":"The displacement is frame-free: the `(L − 1 − i)` in `β_i = λ_i + (L − 1 − i)` cancels, so\n`u_i` is the difference of row lengths and does not depend on the padding. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.sum_betaR_sub_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.sum_betaR_sub_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HookSumElasticity.lean#L104-L116","doc":"**Equal size makes the displacement traceless.**  `2 Σ_{i<L} β_i = 2n + L(L−1)`\n(`two_mul_sum_betaR`), and the second term does not see the shape, so two diagrams of the same\nsize in the same frame have `Σ_i u_i = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.two_mul_sum_hookZ_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.two_mul_sum_hookZ_sub","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HookSumElasticity.lean#L88-L102","doc":"**The difference of two hook sums, in the displacement `u = β(ν) − β(μ)`.**  A linear term\nagainst `r_i = 2β_i(μ) + 1 − 2(L − 1 − 2i)` plus a bare sum of squares — the expansion of the\nseparable quadratic, with nothing dropped and no hypothesis beyond a common frame. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.two_mul_sum_hookZ_separable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HookSum.two_mul_sum_hookZ_separable","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HookSumElasticity.lean#L73-L86","doc":"**The hook sum is separable in β-coordinates.**  No pair term survives:\n\n    2 Σ_{c∈μ} h(c) = Σ_{i<L} [ β_i(β_i + 1) − 2(L − 1 − 2i) β_i ] .\n\nImmediate from `two_mul_sum_hookZ_betaForm` and `sum_pair_betaR_sub`; the content is entirely in\nthe latter, which is where the descending order of the β-set is used. ","signatureChunk":0}]}